WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:02.560
SPEAKER: Let's take a quick
look at how to use Google Cloud

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.360
SQL on the command line.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.170
Go to cloud.google.com and
open up your Cloud console.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.840
Go to the SQL section.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.880
Here you can see your
Cloud SQL instances.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.880
If you don't have a Cloud SQL
instance you can create one.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.910
Click your instance to be taken
to the Instance Overview page.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.230
Now go to the Access Control tab
and then go to the Users tab.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.490
Specify a new root password.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.490
If you don't have the
Google Cloud SDK installed

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.800
on your computer, see the
link in the description

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.150
for how to install it.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.330
Now open your command
line and type gcloud beta

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.420
SQL connect, the name of
your instance, and then

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.590
the username root.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.210
Type in your password
and you'll be

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.733
greeted with the familiar
mySQL command line.

